Chapter: HeapAdvanceRt

 x86 runs in a pre-mapped arena, so advancing the bump cursor over a region
 makes that region writable. A wasm linear memory does not: it starts at its
 declared page count and only `memory.grow` extends it, so a cursor moved past
 the frontier by anything other than the allocator leaves the reservation
 unbacked and the first write into it faults at exactly the memory size. The
 corpus cannot reach this with ordinary allocation, because every ordinary
 allocation goes through the allocator and grows.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   let base = __heap-save
   in let advanced = __heap-advance 67108864
   in let top = __heap-save
   in let wrote-far = poke-byte (top - 8) 0 123
   in let wrote-mid = poke-byte (base + 33554432) 0 77
   in act
    print-line-uni ("advanced by 64 MB " & show (top - base == 67108864))
    print-line-uni ("far byte " & show (peek-byte (top - 8) 0))
    print-line-uni ("mid byte " & show (peek-byte (base + 33554432) 0))
    print-line-uni ("base byte still readable " & show (peek-byte base 0 >= 0))
   end
  end
